<h2>Living with your denture</h2>
<p>Clean your dentures daily, take them out overnight, and come in for a yearly exam so we can check the fit and look at your gums. Gums and bone change shape over time, so most dentures eventually need a reline or replacement. A poorly fitting denture causes sore spots and can speed up bone loss, and both are worth catching early.</p>

<h2>Cost, insurance and financing</h2>
<p>The cost of a denture depends on the type (full, partial or implant-retained), the materials, and whether any extractions are needed first, so we give you a written estimate after your exam.</p>
